{"evt":"note_created","id":"note-mqicz2g835c","workspace":"/Users/imyu/Desktop/zonoid","title":"Codex trace review findings","summary":"Read-only trace review found Codex support works best with explicit session_id, especially CODEX_THREAD_ID, but remains fragile around automatic MCP session inference, hook payload/tool-name parity with Claude-era scripts, hookless worker classification, judging-gate liveness, and Bash multi-target write confinement. Highest-priority fixes: add CODEX_THREAD_ID fallback/integration tests, align post-start/post-lifecycle tool-name matchers with actual Codex Desktop tool names, make /session-info understand agent_tool_spawn same-session workers, require every Bash write target to be inside a claimed worktree, and add live Codex Desktop hook payload fixtures plus end-to-end branch_task/start_task/apply_patch/complete_task coverage.","created_by":"main","valid_from":"2026-06-17T17:42:13.544Z","vec":null,"vecs":null,"actor":"overlay-sync","ts":"2026-06-17T17:42:13.753Z"}
